{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-09-19T07:12:40.307Z","data":{"text":"Task 2 complete.\n\n## Summary\n\n**Changed**\n- `src/harness/types.ts` — added `'measures'` to `HarnessEventType`, the `MeasuresEventData` interface (all required fields plus optional `changedFiles`/`changedLines`/`scopeHashes`), and registered it in `OsqEventData`.\n- `src/watcher/measures.ts` (new, 238 lines) — pure helpers `gatherScopeCounts`, `gatherRepoCounts`, `countImportFanIn`, `countWords`, `countDeltaRequirementsAndScenarios`, `hashFileForMeasures`, `snapshotScopeHashes`, plus the single write path `emitMeasures` and a `gatherStartMeasures` orchestrator.\n- `src/watcher/runner.ts` (196 lines) — gathers and emits the `phase: \"start\"` measures immediately before `spawnTaskAgent`.\n- `tests/measures.test.ts` (new) — 16 tests for every helper, both emission phases, the start aggregator, and a `runTask` integration test.\n\n**Deviations** (detailed in `.run/results/2.md`)\n- Start measures is emitted *before* `spawnTaskAgent` rather than literally after the `started` event; the `started` event is written asynchronously inside `spawn.ts` (out of scope) and task 3 requires the scope-hash baseline before spawn.\n- `emitMeasures(specFolderPath, taskNumber, data)` since `phase` lives on `MeasuresEventData`.\n- Proposal read is inside `measures.ts` to keep `runner.ts` under the enforced <200-line import-graph budget.\n\n**Verification**\n- `node --import tsx --test tests/measures.test.ts` — 16/16 pass\n- `pnpm tsc --noEmit` pass, `pnpm lint` pass\n- `pnpm test` — only the two golden-event fixtures fail, which is task 4's expected job (regenerate fixtures)."}}
